# Self-modifying-code corpus for the lockstep harness's mutant kill
# matrix -- proves QV_MUTANT==9 (FENCE.I doesn't flush, cache
# configuration -- see verification/reference/ref_core.sv). Needs
# --memcfg-b cache explicitly: side A is always flat SRAM (nothing to go
# stale), so this mutant has no opportunity to manifest at all unless
# side B is actually caching. Not part of --corpus all's aggregate for
# the same reason irq.list isn't -- it needs a non-default flag passed
# deliberately, same as --delay-max/--memcfg-b always have.
#
# MAX_RETIRE-based, matching irq.list's own convention (see that file's
# header for the general rationale, though this particular mutant
# doesn't skew timing -- it's a genuine per-retirement RVFI content
# divergence, caught directly by the ordinary comparator at the second
# self-modified call, confirmed empirically at retirement order=15).
#
# target | max_retire (hex file is always verification/lockstep/<target>.hex,
# built via riscv64-unknown-elf-as/ld/objcopy against gen/link.ld,
# matching repro_fencei_smc.s's own documented build commands)
repro_fencei_smc|40
